  "verbalization": "Phomalide appears to have a direct relationship with ZR-75-1 through a series of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Phomalide acts on SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl- and Eryngiolide A. These compounds, in turn, target ZR-75-1, indicating a potential pathway where Phomalide may exert its effects through a shared target, SNU-387. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Phomalide influences SNU-387 and subsequently ZR-75-1 remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central node in the interaction network, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions involved.",
